.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt DTFL-DDIR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl-ddir
.Nd build and run Differential Dataflow IR programs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm run
.Ar program
.Op Ar rows-file
.Nm
.Cm server
.Op Ar session-file
.Nm
.Cm explain
.Ar program
.Op Ar arity
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds and runs programs written in the Differential Dataflow IR (DDIR),
a small language for defining differential dataflows at runtime.
A program names positional input collections, defines derived collections
by expressions
.Pq map, filter, equijoin, reduce, concat, and iterate for recursion ,
and declares named outputs.
A
.Pa .ddp
program uses the pipe syntax
.Pq Ql expr | op | op ;
anything else uses the applicative syntax
.Pq Ql MAP(e, proj), JOIN(e1, e2, proj) .
.Pp
The three subcommands follow the three upstream example programs.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm run Ar program Op Ar rows-file
Evaluate
.Ar program
on explicit input rows and print each export's consolidated contents.
Rows come from
.Ar rows-file ,
or standard input: one row per line, whitespace-separated integers
becoming a tuple of integers, inserted at multiplicity
.Li +1
into the current positional input.
The current input starts at 0; a line
.Ql @ Ns Ar N
selects positional input
.Ar N .
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are skipped.
The output rows are sorted, so a program's result is a stable transcript.
.It Cm server Op Ar session-file
Run the live DDIR server on a command session read from
.Ar session-file ,
or standard input.
Each line is a command:
.Ic install Ar name file ,
.Ic feed Ar prog in# value Oo Ic val Ns = Ns Ar value Oc Oo Ic time Ns = Ns Ar t Oc Oo Ic diff Ns = Ns Ar int Oc ,
.Ic tick ,
.Ic drop Ar name ,
.Ic peek Ar trace Op Ar key ,
.Ic list ,
.Ic help ,
or
.Ic exit .
A line beginning with
.Ql #
or
.Ql --
is a comment.
A
.Ar value
is a comma-separated integer row
.Pq Ql 1,2 No a tuple; Ql _ No or empty, unit ,
or any closed scalar term written without spaces
.Pq Ql tuple(1,2) , Ql list(1,2,3) , Ql inject(2,tuple(3,4)) .
Programs may share results by name: a program's
.Ic export
publishes a trace that a later program's
.Ic import
reads, maintaining a computation incrementally over the producer's output.
Malformed programs and values are reported and the session continues.
.It Cm explain Ar program Op Ar arity
Report
.Ar program
and its explanation rewrite by input and export shape.
The rewrite reports, for a query against a program's output, which input
rows regenerate it.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${datadir}/dtfl/ddir/programs/
The example batch programs
.Pq Pa reach , scc , kcore , stable , adt , binders , unnest .
.It Pa ${datadir}/dtfl/ddir/server/programs/
The example server programs
.Pq producer, consumers, generated-source demos .
.It Pa ${datadir}/dtfl/ddir/server/sessions/
The example server sessions, replayable with
.Nm Cm server .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run reachability over a three-edge graph with one root
.Pq input 0 is edges, input 1 is roots :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf '1 2\\n2 3\\n3 4\\n@1\\n1\\n' | dtfl-ddir run reach.ddir
.Ed
.Pp
Replay the shared-trace session:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl-ddir server shared_trace.txt
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_ddir_parse 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_ddir_server 3
.Sh STANDARDS
Ported from the differential-dataflow
.Ql interactive
crate at tag
.Ql differential-dataflow-v0.25.1 .
.Nm Cm run
is
.Pa examples/ddir_vec.rs ,
.Nm Cm server
is
.Pa examples/ddir_server.rs ,
.Nm Cm explain
is
.Pa examples/dump_explain.rs .
